      "narrative": "Mara Venn's eyes flicker with something \u2014 respect, maybe, that you caught the detail worth chasing. She taps the edge of the sketch again.\n\n\"Before Toran? The lock was Old Bram's domain. He wasn't just the ferryman \u2014 he was the gate's *keeper*. Tended the mechanism himself for decades. Oil on the pins, check the tension on the central tumbler, that sort of thing. Knew every tooth and groove of it like his own knuckles.\"\n\nShe pauses, her thumb brushing the yellowed parchment.\n\n\"But Bram didn't maintain it alone. He apprenticed under a woman named **Sable Quill** \u2014 a courier who used to run messages through the gate when it still opened. She taught him the lock's quirks. The central tumbler? That was her design. Said she'd seen something in the mechanism that needed a custom piece.\"\n\nMara's voice tightens.\n\n\"Sable vanished three months before Bram died. Rode through the gate one morning with a satchel of letters and never came back. Bram took over the lock alone after that. And when he died... Toran Vex inherited the duty. But Toran never learned the *full* trick of it. Just enough to keep the seal intact.\"\n\nShe meets your eyes.\n\n\"Sable Quill is the one who knew that lock best. And she's been gone longer than the gate's been shut.\""
    },
